  "customfield_10187": null,
  "description": "<p>Currently, migration-utilities halts when it encounters an error migrating an object from Fedora 3 to OCFL.  Over the course of a large, long migration, this means that the migration process must be monitored and restarted several times, interventions that increase the amount of time and effort needed to migrate a repository.<br/>\n Proposal:  Add two flags to migration-utils:<br/>\n   --no-halt:  do not halt on error migrating individual objects (default: false)<br/>\n   --max-errors:  only halt after X number of sequential object migration errors (default: no limit)<br/>\n The max-errors flag would only be applicable when no-halt is specified.  The max-errors default would be no limit, i.e., every migration of object would be attempted, regardless of the number of errors that occur in a row.<br/>\n No-halt behavior: if an object-specific migration error is encountered, an ERROR is logged, and the PID of the object is written to a file \"pid/errors.txt\" (alongside \"pid/resume.txt\").  The migration utility then attempts to migrate the next object in the list.<br/>\n Once max-errors is reached (if set), the migration utility logs the ERROR \"Maximum number of sequential errors reached: X\", and then exits.</p>\n\n<p> </p>",
